-- POSITIVE fixture for rule-stdlib-reimpl's delegation exemption (S2-1): a
-- wildcard PARAMETER matched against a hardcoded LITERAL argument is not a
-- delegation -- both `paramNameOf _` and `argNameOf "x"` read `None` at the
-- same position, and comparing the raw `Option String` lists directly would
-- coincidentally "match" on that shared `None`. The rule must keep firing.
import string.{startsWith}

export
startsWithP : String -> String -> Bool
startsWithP _ s = startsWith "x" s
